<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />

    <!-- Theme bootstrap - see the matching comment in base.html. Blocking on
         purpose so [data-theme] and [data-color-scheme] exist before first
         paint. Mirrors loadSavedTheme() in theme-switcher.ts; keep in sync. -->
    <script>
      (function () {
        var d = document.documentElement;
        try {
          d.setAttribute(
            "data-theme",
            localStorage.getItem("kbr-theme") || "base"
          );
          d.setAttribute(
            "data-color-scheme",
            localStorage.getItem("kbr-color-scheme") ||
              (window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches
                ? "dark"
                : "light")
          );
        } catch (e) {
          d.setAttribute("data-theme", "base");
          d.setAttribute("data-color-scheme", "light");
        }
      })();
    </script>

    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>Boundary Conversation Script</title>
    
    <meta name="description" content="A practical script for discussing focus boundaries with your household." />
      
      <link rel="stylesheet" crossorigin href="/assets/index-HASH.css">
</head>

  <body>
    <kbr-navigation>
      <!-- Slotted into .header-content so the switcher sits at the far right
           of the site header. It used to be a fixed-position floating control,
           which overlapped page content at every viewport width. See DF-31. -->
      <kbr-theme-switcher slot="theme-switcher"></kbr-theme-switcher>
    </kbr-navigation>

    <main class="blog-post-layout">
      <aside class="blog-toc-sidebar">
        <div class="blog-toc-sticky-container">
          
          <kbr-table-of-contents></kbr-table-of-contents>
          
        </div>
      </aside>

      <article class="blog-post-content glass-surface">
        <h1 id="boundary-conversation-script">Boundary Conversation Script</h1>

        <div class="blog-post-metadata">
          <div>
            <time datetime="2026-08-01">August 1, 2026</time>
          </div>
        </div>
      <p><em>AI disclosure: This post was generated with AI to help me test the site&#39;s supplementary files features.</em></p>
<p>This script helps you hold a direct but respectful boundary conversation.</p>
<h2 id="conversation-outline">Conversation outline</h2><ol>
<li>State your intent clearly: &quot;I want to protect focused work time and still be fully present after work.&quot;</li>
<li>Describe the impact without blame: &quot;Frequent interruptions make me lose context and delay important work.&quot;</li>
<li>Define the boundary: &quot;From 9-5, assume I am unavailable unless it is urgent.&quot;</li>
<li>Offer a collaboration path: &quot;Let us use our check-in windows for non-urgent topics.&quot;</li>
<li>Confirm and revisit: &quot;Can we try this for a week, then adjust together?&quot;</li>
</ol>
<p>Sibling supplement: <a href="/intentional-work-patterns/supplements/boundary-checklist.html#boundary-checklist">Boundary checklist</a></p>
<p>Back to parent post: <a href="/intentional-work-patterns.html#supplements-heading">Intentional Work Patterns</a></p>

        <kbr-supplement-list></kbr-supplement-list>
        

        <kbr-anchor-copy></kbr-anchor-copy>
      </article>
    </main>

    <!-- Shared markup from templates/partials/footer.html, injected by
         template-processor.ts. Edit the partial, not this line. -->
    <!--
  Shared site footer.

  This is the single source of the footer markup. It is injected into both
  base.html and blog-post.html as the {{{footer}}} template variable, wired up
  in source/builder/template-processor.ts - which is the one choke point both
  the production build and the dev server render through. Do not paste this
  markup into a template; add the variable instead, or every page type grows
  its own copy.

  Light DOM on purpose, not a Lit component: the footer has to be present in
  the generated HTML for crawlers and for readers without JavaScript, and a
  shadow root would leave only an empty custom element in the static output.
-->
<footer class="site-footer">
  <nav class="site-footer-nav" aria-label="Elsewhere on the web">
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a
          href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/kyle-blank-rollins/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >LinkedIn</a
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/KyleBlankRollins/Web-Portfolio"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >GitHub</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
  </nav>
</footer>
      <script type="module" crossorigin src="/assets/index-HASH.js"></script>
    <script type="module" crossorigin src="/assets/lit-HASH.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
